        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T12:47:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a note: free_loaded_vmcs() and other functions are also called in failures cases e.g. in vmx_vcpu_create(), when we probably don\u0027t need to clear the pages.\n\nThat\u0027s probably ok, but that also makes me think: perhaps it\u0027s ok to just _always_ unconditionally clear the pages in __pkvm_hyp_donate_host(), instead of bothering with a flag for that?",
      "revId": "9150cae33a38eab15a2ea1563af809cfc71b02b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a33a8ceb_cdd42b57",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/vmx.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2487,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T13:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Like the comment https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3787907/comment/6ea6b32a_424b05be/ mentioned, we still probably need `__pkvm_hyp_donate_host()` not to clear the memory pages when want to use teardown_mc, as `push_pkvm_memcache` will write physical address to the memory pages. And we also discussed that before at https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3728233/comment/76156533_fa381b12/, we cannot write to these memory pages after donate them. So it is better to let `__pkvm_hyp_donate_host()` to use a flag to determine if to clear or not.",
      "parentUuid": "9230b657_d562efd2",
      "revId": "9150cae33a38eab15a2ea1563af809cfc71b02b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
